[EXPLAIN] Reading the final table
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Sorted from best (most negative) docking score. Look for compounds that are strong in BOTH
  columns (high ML pIC50         and very negative Vina score): those are the best candidates for
  experimental testing. Reference drugs (e.g.         pyrimethamine, methotrexate) give the
  benchmark: a new candidate scoring close to or better than them is interesting;         one far
  worse is probably not worth pursuing even if the ML score is high.
